## NEW: Problem → Solution State Machine (Before/After States)

### Recommended Type: Deterministic Finite Automaton (DFA) for workflow modeling

**Perfect for visualizing the transformation from unprotected to protected states!**

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    title PII Protection Workflow - Before vs After States
    
    [*] --> UnProtected : Extension Installed
    
    state UnProtected {
        direction TB
        [*] --> NoIntercept
        NoIntercept --> ContentCopied: User Ctrl+C
        state "Clipboard = Plain Text" as plain_clipboard
    }

    UnProtected --> Protected : Protection ENABLED
    
    state Protected {
        direction TB
        [*] --> Intercepting
        Intercepting --> PIIDetected: Clipboard Has PII?
        PIIDetected --> PlaceholderGenerated: Category Lookup \\ Apply: [phone:hash], [email:id], etc.
        PlaceholderGenerated --> StoredInDB : Record to Dolt Database
        
        %% This state shows the key difference - transformed clipboard content! 🌟
        note right of Intercepting: ✅ BEFORE this, raw PII flows to apps\n❌ AFTER this, only placeholders remain

    }

    Protected --> Excluded : App in Exclusion List?
    Excluded --> PassThrough : Numbers/App\\Password Manager etc.

    StoredInDB --> RestoreAvailable : User Selects Placeholder Pasted Content  
    RestoreAvailable --> OriginalContentReturned: ⌘⇧E or Auto-detect \\ Fetch from DB

    %% Color coding the states to show transformation phases ⚡
    note right of UnProtected
        🔴 BEFORE STATE\n  • Raw PII exposed in clipboard\\ 
  • Apps see actual phone, email, name\\
  • Security risk at this step!
    end

    note right of Protected  
      🟢 AFTER STATE TRANSFORMATION\\
       * Clipboard contains [phone:a7b8c9d]\\\n  * Only typed characters get through\\\n  • Protection is ON via menu/toggle
    end

```

